# Foundry's scheduled jobs: the source of truth for the VPS `deploy` user's crontab.
#
# Every deploy installs this file between `# BEGIN foundry-managed` / `# END foundry-managed`
# markers (deploy/install-crontab.sh, run by .github/workflows/deploy.yml). Edit it here, never
# with `crontab -e` on the box: a hand edit of a managed line is replaced on the next deploy, and an
# un-marked duplicate of a managed job is removed. Lines outside the markers (the weekly
# db-backup.sh) are left exactly as they are.
#
# Every job goes through run-cron.sh, which reads CRON_SECRET from the app .env and calls the
# route on the internal host. No secret appears on any line here.
#
# src/app/api/cron/__tests__/crontab.test.ts fails if a cron route is in neither this file nor
# UNSCHEDULED_CRONS, or if this file names a route that does not exist.

# Background-job worker, every minute: drains the job queue (curator/foreman runs, client
# archives), plus the monitor watchdog, SSL/domain expiry, the running-month metrics refresh, the
# Monday HR digest, AI-search buyer questions and commitment reads.
* * * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh jobs >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
# Uptime monitors, every minute. Healthy monitors self-throttle to their own interval; a failing
# one is re-checked each minute.
* * * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh wiki-monitors >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
# Big Wedge keep-warm (their free-tier DB) + the watchdog for the hourly course feed.
*/5 * * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh wedge-keepwarm >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
# Pulse: scans left RUNNING after a crash/deploy are salvaged or failed. Was daily (a Vercel Hobby
# limit), so an orphaned scan could spin for up to a day.
*/15 * * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh pulse-reconcile >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
# Pulse monitors: re-scans whichever monitors are due, at most 3 per run. Was daily, which
# capped the whole platform at 3 monitor scans a day.
20 * * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh pulse-run-monitors >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
# Big Wedge course requests, hourly from their API.
15 * * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh wedge-course-feed >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
# CRM lead sync, hourly in working hours (a lead also syncs when someone opens it).
0 8-18 * * 1-5 /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh crm-sync >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1

# Nightly
0 2 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh docs-gdrive-backup >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
0 3 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh auto-archive-tasks >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
30 3 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh member-purge >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
0 6 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh analytics-snapshot >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
0 7 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh embed-conversations >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1

# Working day
0 8,13 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh support-sync >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
30 8 * * 1-5 /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh availability-digest >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
0 9 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh foreman >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
0 9,13 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh meet-transcripts >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
0 10 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh care-digest >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
0 11 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh absence-cover-reconcile >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
# Retention, daily: moves Docs per-section view events older than 60 days to cold storage (at most
# 200 views a run, the cold copy written before the hot rows go). Nothing is deleted for good
# without an admin-approved purge, and it does nothing until a cold store is configured.
30 4 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh retention >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1

# Off-site, encrypted database backup (src/server/db-backup.ts). Does nothing until the
# BACKUP_S3_* bucket and BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY are set. Quiet hours, after the other dailies.
45 3 * * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh db-backup >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
# Monthly restore test of that backup (src/server/db-restore-test.ts): the newest backup is
# restored into the throwaway database foundry_restore_test, counted against production and
# dropped. Off until the same secrets are set. The 2nd, so the 1st's backup is there to test.
15 5 2 * * /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh db-restore-test >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1

# Weekly (Monday 01:00)
0 1 * * 1 /opt/apps/foundry/run-cron.sh curator >> /tmp/foundry-cron.log 2>&1
